---
description: RoleWise project rules (mirrors CLAUDE.md)
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow every rule in `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root. The most important ones:

- Generated content uses only verified `career_facts`. Each claim stores `supporting_fact_ids`.
- No application is submitted without an `approvals` row matching the package hash.
- Personal questions (salary, work authorization, demographics, relocation, start date) go to the user.
- Only allow-listed job sources. No scraping of sites whose terms forbid it.
- No personal data in logs.
- The match score comes from `rolewise/services/matching.py`. The LLM only explains it.
- Every schema change needs an Alembic migration. Every API edge uses Pydantic schemas.
- Frontend calls the backend only through `apps/web/lib/api.ts`.
